-- title:
--   Smooth-point stalk from an affine chart, supersingular component, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa(A),M')$ over the residue field $\kappa(A)$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'$, with a chosen element $s\in W$, and assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ inside the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ such that every $a\in A$ differs from some element of $k_0\cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$, and assume $\kappa(A)$ is algebraically closed. Let $K_b$ be the bottom intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, let $A_b$ be the valuation subring of $K_b$ consisting of the elements lying in $A$, assumed a henselian discrete valuation ring, and let $\varpi_b\neq 0$ generate its maximal ideal. Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is then: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'/k_0$ and valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is everything, and such that for each finite extension $K'/k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ any $K'$-linearly independent family $c_0,\dots,c_{m-1}$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ admits no nontrivial relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ with $a_i$ in the compositum $k_0(K')\!\cdot\!F_0$; for every subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ carrying an $A_b$-algebra structure compatible with the inclusions, with $B$ contained in the compositum $k_0(K_b)\!\cdot\! F_0$ and every element of that compositum of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, with $B$ formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, with $\mathrm{Ring.KrullDimLE}\,1$ for $B/\varpi_bB$, with $B$ contained in $W_0$, with $\varpi_b$ mapping to a prime element of $B$, and with $W_0$ the localisation of $B$ at that prime (an element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ iff it is $g/h$ with $\varpi_b\nmid h$); and for every field $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa(A)$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with values in $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with surjective residue map onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, cutting out $A$ on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) such that $R.\mathrm{integers}$ meets $F_0$ exactly in $W_0$ and contains $B$, with every element of $F_{ss}$ a quotient of residues of elements of $B$, and for every place $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa(A)$ whose valuation subring contains all residues of elements of $B$: there exist a subring $S$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, a ring homomorphism $\varphi:A_b[X]\to S$ and a ring homomorphism $\chi:S\to\kappa(A)$ such that $S$ contains the image of $A_b$ and $\varphi(C\,a)$ is that image of $a$, $\chi(\varphi(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa(A)$, $\chi(\varphi(X))=0$, $S$ is local with $\ker\chi$ its maximal ideal, $S$ lies in the compositum $k_0(K_b)\!\cdot\!F_0$ and every element of that compositum is a quotient of elements of $S$, $\varphi$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type, $S\subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$ with an element of $S$ lying in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ precisely when it is divisible by $\varphi(C\,\varpi_b)$, the $R$-residue of any element of $S$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and reduces there to the image of its $\chi$-value in the residue field of $Q$, the invariant $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ of the $R$-residue of $\varphi(X)$ equals $1$, $B\subseteq S$, and $S$ consists exactly of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ whose denominator has $R$-residue with nonzero reduction at $Q$.
--
--   This provides, at a smooth point of the supersingular component of the reduction of the full-level modular curve in characteristic $q=3$, the local ring of the model read off an affine chart, together with an étale coordinate over the base discrete valuation ring and the residue character at the point, the coordinate being a uniformiser at the corresponding place. It is the $q=3$ case of the construction used when assembling the base smooth-point stalks of the semistable model, and is cited by the declarations that build those stalks and their localisations.
